url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  Open, reproducible benchmark for multichannel telemetry anomaly detection.
  Synthetic 512-channel signals are split into sixteen 32-channel blocks and
  scored by block-level detectors behind a plugin API: the transparent OES32
  reference detector (0.45 max|x| + 0.35 RMS + 0.20 mean|x|), a robust
  z-score baseline, EWMA and CUSUM temporal detectors, and an optional
  Isolation Forest. Version 0.2.0 adds multi-step synthetic streams and a
  scorecard in which every detector's threshold is calibrated the same way on
  held-out clean data, reporting false-positive rate, recall, exact
  localization, IoU, detection latency and machine-dependent CPU time.
  Synthetic data only; not quantum, not GPS, not a physical sensor, and no
  performance claims about real systems.
keywords:
  - anomaly-detection
  - benchmark
